#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "67da2ffa-b472-5084-985c-dde4cd2df661" :question/math-academy-id "e-5219" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/57/57ec3c089f80e2d35d9b83f6791eefca9b452d933f82209ed434d35d77b78788.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087532 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "e01914e2-b4f0-52b5-baf1-8b7fa5da3f18" :question/math-academy-id "e-5222" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/b6/b6eb2c0222181eaa4eb2a1c232fdf2eee905ab0e0a8a9c2284911ab8dd26cade.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087533 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "10dda4fa-e047-53f4-a20a-b881e14f3e2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5223" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{25} + \\dfrac{(y+2)^2}{16} = 1,$ find its center, and the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=2$ and $k=-2,$ so the center is located at $(2,-2).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have $a^2=25$ and $b^2=16.$\n\n- Since $a^2=25,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$\n\n- Since $b^2=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a = 2\\cdot5 = 10,$ and the minor axis has length $2b = 2\\cdot4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6450c4-26cb-5ace-8d0f-74623d6f7b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247826} {:answer/id #uuid "767bf4cf-2491-555a-ab30-52ebadad4d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248467} {:answer/id #uuid "c66fa7de-7fc5-5e9a-8fd6-4363ca207aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249188} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1ba8c7-2fd2-54e4-909b-7a53b0fb5e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249512} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee4f54-cd71-5df4-9686-16c0143c4fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee4f54-cd71-5df4-9686-16c0143c4fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249593} :answer-field/id #uuid "403fe98d-e127-5b86-836f-fbcff7e95447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "390b2e5b-addf-5887-a46a-a83def8e8ae2" :question/math-academy-id "q-115286" :question/problem "![](images/07/07003c76b7939be373eb4b1dc810e721f44b8c0405ee5312fd211f3b9959634b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-4,3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9e4e68f-490a-50ec-831b-a2606c9e2e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9e4e68f-490a-50ec-831b-a2606c9e2e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293914} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6cc6684-109c-5446-8ce1-df88d1548753" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "769c3ba1-be44-5d72-ab21-003c024cdeed" :question/math-academy-id "q-278251" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6bb7a8dc9b34c03e5456b84b843c8975aac8ec8f09135fe9069693febc24ba78.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "292efafb-266a-58e4-94e5-9af834924ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "292efafb-266a-58e4-94e5-9af834924ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293109} :answer-field/id #uuid "a587ca80-28e2-5845-8830-3ac36c072a3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1f1fe35-990c-50d4-ada2-aab504633e3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-278254" :question/problem "![](images/65/65a76a438b3459a92db0e00b0c9bd281b8a9c58fa68afd2d8e6468a1d99b1cf9.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b9b649-efc6-5e5d-a230-ee6e7ce02461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b9b649-efc6-5e5d-a230-ee6e7ce02461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293097} :answer-field/id #uuid "e342221d-038c-51b2-85c4-c859ed5009fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85edbeb0-9eb4-5dad-b06c-14fbea0c087e" :question/math-academy-id "q-278477" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb178149bac4d1fcfd0690b7005f263c3647488ac86ed70f1143540e23e04b6e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y+2)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89bfade5-62c5-5587-8dee-ea7102a413ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 2)^{2})/(16) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(4) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086623} {:answer/id #uuid "933c3687-01ce-5daf-97d5-27e4db4fa9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 1)^{2})/(16) + ((y - 2)^{2})/(4) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086624} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3988a9-c489-5c19-b24e-9e515471fde9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 1)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 2)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086625} {:answer/id #uuid "04323df2-7d69-5b03-82cc-81d0b414ab2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 2)^{2})/(16) + ((y - 1)^{2})/(4) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086626} {:answer/id #uuid "2400fb48-4c53-5942-be1a-0fc2c2147618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 1)^{2})/(16) + ((y + 2)^{2})/(4) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086627}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4e366f3a-7c2a-578a-a16e-93376dc6e782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086622}] :question/id #uuid "b4710d3d-38f7-5357-85e6-50fcb09ce908" :question/math-academy-id "q-7623" :question/problem "![](images/91