lty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71b997b6-5617-5e73-9fb1-047d1816753f" :question/math-academy-id "q-7624" :question/problem "![](images/47/4741a7b8b46972ed29cf85f747037e3e452049e97a6f5833a96e8de34d7b494e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
